  "name": "uuidna per-level report — reach, cost and fidelity",
  "description": "Every level of the datapath — hexbit tile, handle, uuid, sealed ledger — on the host that ran the generator. Three axes per level, each figure carrying the technique it was determined by: REACH (declared by construction, citing the level's sealed theorem), COST (steady-state floor, measured) and FIDELITY (disagreements with Lean-sealed values over a stated execution count, measured; a bound, never a proof of zero). Sealed keys cited: usable_gap_is_two_to_eighty (128 - 48 = 80), n_qubit_dimension (n qubits span 2^n amplitudes), gate_error_baseline_class (1000 = 10^3 per million).",
  "url": "https://uuidna.com/quantum-advantage.jsonld",
